Purpose:
Suppress workbench popup/toast/bell notifications and record them to a
server-side log (POST /notify-log, see src/node/routes/notifyLog.ts) instead.

The feature is controlled at startup by the CS_DISABLE_NOTIFICATIONS
environment variable and is ENABLED BY DEFAULT. Set it to "false" or "0" to
restore the upstream notification behavior:

  CS_DISABLE_NOTIFICATIONS=false

The equivalent --disable-notifications option is accepted in three places:
- environment variable: CS_DISABLE_NOTIFICATIONS=false (or 0)
- config file (e.g. ~/.config/code-server/config.yaml): disable-notifications: false
- command line: --disable-notifications=false (a bare flag enables)
An explicit CLI/config value takes priority over the environment variable.
Support for "--boolean-flag=false" was added to the CLI parser in
src/node/cli.ts so a YAML `false` value is honored (outside this patch).

How it works:
- src/node/cli.ts reads the env var (default: enabled) and forwards
  "disable-notifications" to the VS Code server arguments.
- serverEnvironmentService.ts registers the new boolean server argument.
- webClientServer.ts exposes it to the workbench via
  productConfiguration.disableNotifications.
- product.ts adds disableNotifications to IProductConfiguration.
- notificationService.ts injects IProductService: while the flag is on
  (default), notify() logs the notification to /notify-log and returns a
  NoOpNotification; when off, the upstream notify() implementation runs
  unchanged. info()/warn()/error() route through notify() so the switch
  covers all severities.

Verify:
- Default, or CS_DISABLE_NOTIFICATIONS=true: trigger a notification (for
  example an extension error); no toast/bell/badge surfaces and a JSON line is
  appended to <data-dir>/notification.log.
- CS_DISABLE_NOTIFICATIONS=false: notifications render exactly as upstream and
  no /notify-log requests are issued.

Related:
- The /notify-log route is implemented in src/node/routes/notifyLog.ts and
  registered in src/node/routes/index.ts (outside this patch).
- This patch is independent: hunks only anchor on upstream context lines.

